{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And showing kindness to thousands of those who love.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: to those who act out of love. And what is written (Exodus 20:6) — לאוהביו ולשומרי מצותיו — 'to those who love Him and keep His commandments,' to a thousand generations — refers to those who act out of fear. And thus they said: this one is interpreted in light of what is adjacent to it, and that one is interpreted in light of what is adjacent to it — for even though the service of those who act out of fear is not complete, nevertheless their reward reaches as far as the heavens. And thus our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in the chapter מקום שנהגו: it is written ״כי גדול עד שמים״ — 'for it is great as far as the heavens' (Psalms 108:5), and it is written (Psalms 57:11) ״מעל שמים״ — 'above the heavens.' It is not difficult: here refers to those who act לשמה (for its own sake), here refers to those who act שלא לשמה (not for its own sake). And like what Rav said, for Rav said: a person should always engage in Torah and commandments even שלא לשמן (not for their own sake), for from שלא לשמן one comes לשמן (for their own sake). Those who act לשמן are those who act out of love; those who act שלא לשמן are those who do not act out of love but out of fear. And what they said in Berakhot — 'anyone who engages in Torah שלא לשמה, it would have been better for him had he not been created' — that refers to one who does not act at all out of love but only out of fear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:25.568248842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}